# Copy to .env (or .env.production) and fill in before `npm run build` for a
# real Solana deployment. See CSP-AUDIT.md's Content-Security-Policy section.

# --- Solana-only: RPC endpoint baked into the build -------------------------
#
# The RPC node lib/chain.ts's Connection reads/broadcasts against, AND the
# origin vite.config.ts's injectCsp plugin bakes into the built index.html's
# CSP meta tag (`connect-src 'self' <this origin>`). Build-time only — the
# server no longer supplies an RPC URL via GET /api/v1/config — because a
# browser CSP can only allow-list an origin it's told about at build time.
#
# Unlike investor-web's VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL (a genuine trust-boundary pin
# against a compromised server), this is purely a CSP-mechanics requirement
# for the admin console: the Go server serves this very bundle, so the RPC
# endpoint baked into it is already server-trusted either way.
#
# Irrelevant (leave unset) for an EVM deployment — connect-src is then just
# 'self'.
#
# The CSP also sets upgrade-insecure-requests, which the browser applies to
# every connect-src origin except loopback hosts (localhost/127.0.0.1) — a
# NON-loopback plain http:// endpoint is silently rewritten to https:// and
# then fails to connect, since the RPC node doesn't serve TLS there (audit-10
# L-06). buildCsp() (see lib/cspPolicy.ts) throws at build time if this is set
# to a non-loopback http:// URL, so a real (non-localhost) deployment MUST use
# https://. Plain http:// is only valid here for a loopback host.
#
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=http://localhost:8899

# --- Solana-only: WebSocket endpoint baked into the build --------------------
#
# The Connection's subscription transport (confirmTransaction and any account
# subscriptions — see lib/chain.ts's waitForSolanaSignature) opens a
# WebSocket connection, which is a DIFFERENT origin from the HTTP RPC above
# (web3.js otherwise derives one by swapping the scheme and bumping the port
# by one, e.g. http://localhost:8899 -> ws://localhost:8900). Baked into the
# same CSP connect-src as VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL (see vite.config.ts's injectCsp
# and cspPolicy.ts). Leaving this unset does NOT disable confirmation — it
# just means the Connection falls back to web3.js's derived WS endpoint,
# which then will NOT be covered by the CSP and confirmations will be
# blocked by the browser; always set it alongside
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL for a real Solana deployment.
#
# Same loopback rule as VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL above applies here: a non-loopback
# plain ws:// URL is rejected at build time — use wss:// for anything other
# than a loopback host.
#
# VITE_SOLANA_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8900
